            <ArticleTitle>The role of peripheral opiate antagonists in pain medicine and perioperative care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>540-7, 533-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Pre-clinical and clinical trials of peripheral opiate antagonists have shed new light on the effects of exogenous and endogenous opioids.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONTENTS" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">This article review preclinical studies and clinical opioid bowel disfunction trials.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">If approved these drugs may offer potential solutions to important clinical problems in pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
